# requirements/investigate/investigate.ears
# Companion set from "Investigate: Field to Candidate on the STScI Ecosystem" §10 (docs/investigate.md).
capability: Investigate a field
owner: investigate
requirements:
  - id: INV-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The system shall run Investigate only over a declared Field and a versioned, hashed test profile."
    rationale: "A profile frozen and hashed before the run cannot be tuned against its own output."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-002
    pattern: event
    text: "When Investigate starts, the system shall record the field, the profile hash, the archive releases consulted, the code revision and the seed in an investigation-set manifest."
    rationale: "An exploratory run is reproducible and auditable like an experiment."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-003
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The identification service shall give every identified object an identification record naming the method, the image or catalogue it came from, and the matched Gaia source key or null."
    rationale: "Every object says how it was found; an unmatched detection is flagged, not dropped."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-004
    pattern: event
    text: "When objects are identified, the system shall retrieve catalogue rows and observation indices only through ArchiveGateway and ObservationArchiveGateway."
    rationale: "Two ports, cassettes in CI, one weekly live smoke per adapter. The SIMBAD resolver and the VO registry travel through the same Transport and cassettes, and the weekly live smoke asks each Investigate service one question at the Pleiades and records the answers."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T0, T3]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The kernel shall register every retrieved row set and product as a DatasetArtifact with source release, licence and citation before any test reads it."
    rationale: "Tests read registered evidence only, so a result is reproducible from the artifacts alone. A product a dialect curates is registered as the curated child of its raw parent, naming the dialect and its version; its first line stamps both, so equal rows from two raw products stay two artifacts with their own lineage. A product offered as two types is fetched and registered once."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-006
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The kernel shall run only tests that are registered TaskKinds with a CPU reference implementation and a declared null model."
    rationale: "Nothing outside the registry runs, and every test has an empirical false-positive rate."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-007
    pattern: event
    text: "When tests complete, the system shall open one Investigation per candidate above the ranking threshold and record the number of objects and tests examined for the set."
    rationale: "The multiplicity is recorded so false-discovery control can be applied at set level. The ranking policy names its ranker: significance is the kernel's own, stellar is the stellar module's CandidateRanker, and a policy with no ranker is refused before anything runs, never silently swapped."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-008
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The kernel shall label every investigation result EXPLORATORY and give it no Verdict."
    rationale: "Investigate is how candidates are found, never how a claim is verified."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-009
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If an investigation is promoted without a frozen confirmatory predeclaration that names evidence the investigation did not use, then the kernel shall refuse the promotion and record the refusal."
    rationale: "Exploratory results must not leak into confirmatory claims."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-010
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The kernel shall retain parked and closed investigations with their dossiers and reasons."
    rationale: "The set is as much evidence as the candidates."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-011
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a bound ecosystem package is imported outside sdp.adapters or the domain-library allow-list, then the architecture test shall fail the build."
    rationale: "Each ecosystem package is bound once, behind one port, with a fake and a contract suite: photutils behind SourceDetector, tweakwcs behind WcsRefiner."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T0]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-012
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The field viewer plugin shall render the results of InvestigateField and contain no analysis logic or archive calls."
    rationale: "The Imviz plugin is a driving adapter; heavy work stays in the kernel's runner."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T0, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-013
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where a cloud URI is available for a MAST product, the system shall record the URI and the checksum of the bytes actually read."
    rationale: "What was read is what is cited."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-014
    pattern: event
    text: "When the evidence UI sends a triage step, the API shall apply only park, reopen, close or annotate, record its actor and reason, and refuse promotion."
    rationale: "Scientists triage without a terminal; promotion needs a frozen confirmatory predeclaration and stays on the CLI (INV-009)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-015
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The evidence UI shall show the exact sdp command for every signed step rather than perform it."
    rationale: "Freezing, approval, promotion and above-threshold plan approval are signed with a personal key (ADR-004, INT-014)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-016
    pattern: event
    text: "When Identify resolves a field through a resolver that can resolve a whole field, the kernel shall ask it once for every identified position and record the same record by_position gives for each."
    rationale: "SIMBAD star by star costs one to two seconds a star and dominated every run; one field query plus batched bibliographies takes seconds (#65)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_investigate::test_a_field_resolver_is_asked_once_for_the_whole_field_with_the_same_answers"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_investigate_vo::test_a_field_is_resolved_from_one_box_query_nearest_first_then_lower_oid"
  - id: INV-017
    pattern: event
    text: "When an acquisition or an Investigate stage completes, the system shall report the bytes it added to the artifact store, counting an artifact that was already stored as zero, together with an acquisition's archive requests and rows."
    rationale: "A stress run needs to know what each pull cost in disk and calls without measuring it by hand (#60)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_metrics::test_acquire_reports_rows_bytes_requests_and_time_and_a_reread_costs_nothing"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_metrics::test_a_run_reports_seconds_and_stored_bytes_per_stage"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_metrics::test_the_meter_counts_equal_bytes_once"
  - id: INV-018
    pattern: event
    text: "When the evidence UI asks the API to execute an approved plan in the background, the API shall answer before the run ends and report the run as running, finished or failed with its error on the plan."
    rationale: "A JWST plan reads archives for 10 to 20 minutes, longer than a browser or the UI server waits for one answer (undici gives up after 5 minutes). The run continues on a worker thread; asking again while it runs starts nothing new, and a failed run can be started again because the plan stays approved. Jobs live in the API process, so a restart forgets a running job but not the plan."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-019
    pattern: event
    text: "When the evidence UI asks the API to register the archives, the API shall read every source's descriptor as a background job and list the registered sources with their verification dates."
    rationale: "A fresh installation plans nothing until the descriptors are registered (INT-017), and reading MAST's from the VO takes minutes. A scientist starts it once from the Start page instead of a terminal (`sdp integration register` does the same)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-020
    pattern: event
    text: "When a field investigation has read images, the API shall list each image with its envelope's validation checks and every Gaia star the image-counterpart test placed on it, with the star's predicted and matched pixels, its chance probability and whether the match was ambiguous, and serve the image as a picture with its pixel rows upright (y increasing upward)."
    rationale: "The scientist checks a JWST field by eye: Gaia's stars drawn where their motion puts them on the calibrated image, flagged and ambiguous ones first, beside the checks the FITS file passed (INT-019). The test records the pixels in the aligned frame, so the viewer needs no WCS and draws nothing the test did not compute; the picture is an asinh stretch and is never read by a test."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-021
    pattern: event
    text: "When a scientist saves a field investigation's evidence dossier, the system shall write one RO-Crate holding the set manifest, each stage's output as stored, the acquisition plan with its approval, every candidate with its triage history and dossier, each image drawn with its Gaia stars marked, and every artifact the stages name under the SHA-256 of its bytes."
    rationale: "The journey ends with evidence a colleague can check without SDP's database or any archive (docs/investigate.md: the dossier exports as an RO-Crate). Stage outputs keep their stored bytes so each hashes to the id the manifest records; the images carry the same overlay the app draws (INV-020). The label stays EXPLORATORY. `sdp investigate bundle`, the API and the app's Save button all build it the same way."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-022
    pattern: event
    text: "When a scientist reproduces a field investigation from its evidence dossier, the system shall verify every file's checksum, re-run the Test stage over the dossier's products with the recorded profile and seed, and report every result that differs from the recorded one beyond the tests' numerical tolerance."
    rationale: "A saved dossier is reproducible only if the Test stage can be run again from it alone. The rerun reads no database and no archive, so it runs on any installation with the same tests registered; a broken file, a profile that no longer hashes to its recorded hash, or a missing product refuses the reproduction instead of comparing against something else, and so does a stage file that is not the output the manifest names by hash. Each result is compared within its own test's tolerance, and every result for one subject is compared, not only the last. Re-running the image tests on a real JWST field takes minutes (5.5 for the M92 field), so the API runs the check as a job (INV-018), one reproduction at a time, and the app reads its report when it has finished."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-023
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The Candidates stage shall store every candidate's dossier under its logical path before it saves the investigation that names the dossier."
    rationale: "Each dossier is a few small synced files. Written one after another, Stage 2 of the stress run (#67, 16,777 candidates on 1.7 million stars) spent 57 minutes in this stage waiting on the disk while the CPU sat idle, slowing as the folder grew. The dossiers are now written by several writers side by side (DOSSIER_WRITERS); every write finishes, and any failure is raised, before an investigation naming a dossier is saved."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_investigate::test_candidate_dossiers_are_written_side_by_side_and_each_is_named_by_its_investigation"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_investigate::test_a_failed_dossier_write_stops_the_stage_before_any_investigation_is_saved"
  - id: INV-024
    pattern: event
    text: "When a scientist asks to compare a candidate with reference catalogues, the system shall query each chosen catalogue for one cone around the candidate's position, moved along its proper motion to each catalogue's epoch, and keep every answer with the investigation, with who asked, when, the cone, the catalogue's release and citation, its rows within the cone nearest first under canonical names, the archive's raw answer as an artifact, and the reason when a catalogue did not answer, without changing the candidate's results, rank, state or the evidence it used."
    rationale: "Before writing a confirmatory predeclaration the scientist rules out 'already known' and 'artefact' by putting the candidate beside SIMBAD, Gaia DR3, 2MASS, AllWISE, Pan-STARRS DR2 and AAVSO VSX on one page. A pull is context, not evidence a test read, so it cannot affect INV-008/INV-009; pulls are appended, never replaced, so the comparison a scientist relied on stays on record. One catalogue that is down fails only its own pull. SIMBAD and VSX fail over to CDS's mirrors (DSI-017), and each pull waits at most about 90 s per attempt so a scientist is never left waiting on a dead archive for long."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INV-025
    pattern: optional
    text: "Where a profile names an installed clustering algorithm for the astrometric-coherence test, the system shall find that test's clusters, on the field and on every shuffled field, with the named algorithm, record the algorithm with every cluster, and refuse a name that is not installed before the investigation opens."
    rationale: "The stress run (#67) spent 50 minutes in the Test stage: about 4,200 HDBSCAN searches on 13,928 Praesepe stars at about 0.98 s each with scikit-learn's HDBSCAN. fast-hdbscan (the sweep's Boruvka HDBSCAN, #136) takes about 0.015 s and agreed on the field (ARI 0.999 to 1.0, same contrast) but chose a different best cluster on 2 of 15 shuffled fields, which can move a p-value. So scikit-learn stays the default, as UC-01's predeclared reference, and a profile opts in to another installed algorithm by id under `clusterer`. Every cluster records the algorithm that found it, so a result is never read as UC-01's when it is not."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_field_tests::test_a_profile_names_another_installed_clusterer_and_an_unknown_one_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_field_tests::test_every_cluster_records_the_algorithm_the_profile_chose"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_field_tests::test_a_clusterer_that_is_not_installed_is_refused_before_the_investigation_opens"
  - id: INV-026
    pattern: event
    text: "When a profile runs the cross-survey-contradiction test, the system shall score each star by its largest disagreement with Gaia, among the survey comparisons it counts, against an uncertainty budget calibrated on the field."
    rationale: "Matching only says several surveys saw the same star; Leigh asked (2026-10-31) for the measurements that disagree beyond their expected uncertainties. 2MASS positions are single-night, so the prediction includes the parallax shift on that night (checked against astropy's Earth ephemeris to 0.02 of the parallax). Main had no test comparing one star's own measurements across surveys: photometric-corroboration fits one colour against the field, image- and exposure-counterpart check positions for one survey pair each. Canonical 2MASS and Pan-STARRS rows carry no per-row errors yet, so the budget adds to whatever errors a row reports the extra scatter the field shows, solved per G-magnitude bin (median start, then a 3-sigma clipped mean), and p-values use Student's t or F with the bin's star count because that budget is an estimate: on the synthetic field the null false-alarm rate is 1.1 to 1.4 percent at alpha 0.01, against 3.5 percent with normal tails. Comparisons a survey cannot resolve (a neighbour within 2.5 mag inside its resolution at the survey's epoch), bands the survey flags as poor or leaves ungraded, Pan-STARRS rows of fewer than three detections, and channels with too few stars are set aside with their reason, never counted. The worst counted z is Sidak-corrected over the comparisons counted, and every comparison is written into the result with its budget terms."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction::test_the_planted_contradictions_are_found_and_labelled"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction::test_the_field_is_not_flagged_once_its_budget_is_calibrated"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction::test_a_blend_is_set_aside_with_its_reason_and_never_counted"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction::test_null_fields_stay_near_the_nominal_false_positive_rate"
  - id: INV-027
    pattern: event
    text: "When the cross-survey-contradiction test compares a 2MASS or Pan-STARRS measurement with Gaia, the system shall start that comparison's uncertainty budget from the error the archive reports for the measurement."
    rationale: "INV-026 had to let the field set the whole budget because canonical 2MASS and Pan-STARRS rows carried no per-row errors, so a faint star with a large real error and a bright star with a small one were judged by the same bin-wide scatter. The 2mass-psc and ps1-dr2 dialects (1.2.0) now keep the archive's own errors in quality_flags when a fetch asks for them: 2MASS j/h/k_msigcom and the 1-sigma error ellipse err_maj/err_min, Pan-STARRS g to y PSF magnitude errors and raMeanErr/decMeanErr, plus Pan-STARRS z and y magnitudes. They are optional columns, so a profile written before them still curates to the rows it always did. A position error is the root mean square of the two the archive gives, per axis. A missing value, Pan-STARRS's -999, a zero or an implausibly large error counts as no reported error, and the field's calibration term then carries the budget as before. With the true errors reported on the synthetic field the calibration term falls below 0.6 of the reported error and the null false-alarm rate stays under 2.5 percent at alpha 0.01."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_errors::test_the_error_columns_are_optional_and_kept_when_fetched"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_errors::test_a_fetch_without_them_curates_to_the_rows_it_always_did"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_errors::test_the_comparisons_carry_the_archive_s_errors"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_errors::test_with_the_true_errors_reported_the_field_adds_little"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_errors::test_null_fields_with_reported_errors_stay_near_the_nominal_rate"
  - id: INV-028
    pattern: event
    text: "When a profile running the cross-survey-contradiction test fetches AllWISE rows or Hubble or Webb images, the system shall compare each Gaia star's position and brightness there with Gaia's prediction under the same field-calibrated budget as the other surveys."
    rationale: "Leigh's ask (2026-10-31) named Gaia, JWST, Hubble and infrared measurements; PR 1 and PR 2 covered 2MASS and Pan-STARRS. AllWISE (allwise-psd dialect, IRSA allwise_p3as_psd) adds a 2010 position and W1/W2: its 6-arcsec beam sets the blend distance, a band whose cc_flags letter is not 0 is set aside as contaminated (and the position when either band is), and a resolved galaxy (ext_flg above 0) is set aside whole. AllWISE's basic columns do not carry each source's mean epoch, so the dialect uses MJD 55400 (2010.5558) for every row; the half-year spread is 50 mas for a star moving 100 mas/yr, inside AllWISE's own errors. Each Hubble or Webb image is aligned to Gaia and described by the photometer as epoch-change does (INT-025, shared prepare_frame), then each star gets a brightness, forced photometry in one FWHM at its counterpart with an instrumental magnitude the field's colour relation calibrates, and a position, its counterpart's, the nearest detection within image_search_arcsec. A star is set aside when a neighbour no more than blend_delta_mag fainter sits within the aperture radius plus one FWHM, when its counterpart is ambiguous (a second detection less than one FWHM further, or a detection another star also claims), or when it is saturated or masked; a star with no counterpart gets no comparison on that image, because an aperture where Gaia puts it reads only the background. The detector's centroid error is a rough guess, so the field sets the image position budget. On the synthetic four-camera field a star 0.7 mag brighter and one 0.4 arcsec out of place are flagged on both images, a pair WFC3 merged is set aside there and compared on NIRCam, and the null false-alarm rate stays under 2.5 percent at alpha 0.01, as it does with AllWISE added to the catalogue field."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_warm_dust_excess_in_both_wise_bands_is_flagged"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_band_allwise_flags_as_contaminated_is_set_aside_with_the_position"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_row_allwise_fits_as_extended_is_set_aside_whole"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_null_fields_with_allwise_stay_near_the_nominal_rate"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_star_brighter_on_the_images_is_flagged_in_both"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_star_displaced_on_the_images_is_flagged_by_position"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_pair_the_detector_could_not_split_is_a_blend_where_it_was_not_split"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_star_no_image_shows_gets_no_comparison_on_it"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_an_image_that_cannot_be_aligned_is_named_and_left_out"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_a_moved_star_is_measured_where_it_is_so_its_brightness_agrees"
      - "python/tests.investigate.test_cross_survey_contradiction_channels::test_null_fields_on_the_images_hold_the_rate_near_alpha"
  - id: INV-029
    pattern: event
    text: "When a candidate's dossier holds a cross-survey-contradiction result, the system shall show each of its comparisons with the measurement, Gaia's prediction, the difference, the expected scatter and the verdict on the candidate page, the compare page and the set dossier's README."
    rationale: "INV-026 to INV-028 write every comparison and its budget into the result, but until now a scientist saw only the test's p-value. The candidate page gains a 'Do the surveys agree?' section: a one-sentence summary (what disagreed, by how much, how many times the expected scatter, and the pattern's reading), then one row per comparison, flagged first, then those that agree, then those set aside with their reason. Positions read in mas with a direction after the field's own offset is removed; image magnitudes are called instrumental. The compare page shows the same rows, without those that agree, above the catalogue table, so the engine's findings and the reference catalogues sit side by side. The set dossier's README lists each judged candidate with its pattern and p, and each flagged comparison with its difference and z. The UI tests run on results the Python engine wrote for its synthetic field (src/lib/testing/contradictions.json)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T2]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "typescript/packages/evidence-ui/test/contradictions.test.ts::[INV-029] puts the flagged comparison first and says how it differs"
      - "typescript/packages/evidence-ui/test/contradictions.test.ts::[INV-029] says in one sentence what disagreed, by how much, and how to read it"
      - "typescript/packages/evidence-ui/test/contradictions.test.ts::[INV-029] names the reason a comparison was set aside"
      - "python/tests.usecase.test_set_dossier_contradictions::test_each_flagged_comparison_is_listed_under_its_candidate"
